  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates skewness based on whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to favorable outcomes. In this case, Lottery A is more left-skewed (34% vs. 33% favorable probability). However, the individual did not mention skewness or the distribution of probabilities across outcomes in terms of favorability. Instead, they focused on the near-equivalence of probabilities and the slightly higher monetary value of Lottery B. Their justification is based on maximizing monetary gain given similar probabilities, which aligns more with expected value or a simple comparison of outcomes and probabilities rather than skewness. There is no indication that the individual considered or weighed the relative mass of probability assigned to favorable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason (skewness preference) was not used in the deliberation process described. The individual’s reasoning is inconsistent with the skewness-based rule.",
